      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Receptionist/KTIS - Minnesota, United States Careers Home Declaration of Christian Community Doctrinal Statement Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Receptionist/KTIS Minnesota, United States Staff PT Nonexempt Add to favorites View favorites Title: Receptionist/KTIS VP Area: VP - Media Department: KTIS - St Paul Position Compensation: $20.50 - $22.85 / hour Location: St. Paul, Minnesota - Home Office, KTIS, Faith Media Who We Are: Northwestern is a faith-driven community, UNWavering in our Christ-centered principles and identity as those who profess faith in Jesus. Rooted in the unshakable foundation of God’s Word and our calling to impact His world, our mission and vision flow from these core values, expressed through Christ-centered higher education at the University of Northwestern – St. Paul and through gospel outreach and faithfulness with Northwestern Media. Position Summary: To support the mission of KTIS by serving as a welcoming and professional first point of contact for listeners, donors, and guests, while providing administrative support for daily office operations and demonstrating Christ-like hospitality and integrity in every interaction. This is a part-time position scheduled for 20 hours per week. Key Responsibilities: • Guest Relations: Serve as the primary point of contact for listeners, donors, guests, and callers by providing professional, timely, and welcoming service, and ensuring inquiries are appropriately addressed or directed. • Office Support: Support efficient day-to-day office operations by maintaining a welcoming front-office environment and assisting with administrative and operational tasks. • Administrative Assistance: Provide administrative assistance through project support, coordination of assigned activities, and completion of general office tasks. • Perform other duties as assigned. Because our community is a significant part of our mission and the development of our students and listeners, all employees serve as ministers of the gospel of Jesus Christ by actively partnering with the University to disciple students as they grow intellectually and spiritually, and with Northwestern Media to lead people to Christ and nurture believers to maturity in their faith. Qualifications: Required: • High School diploma or GED equivalent • Minimum of one year related professional administrative experience • Maintain a growing, personal relationship with Jesus Christ, reflect His character in all interactions, and faithfully uphold and embrace Northwestern’s mission, Doctrinal Statement and Declaration of Christian Community Key Skills: • Independent & Teamwork: Capable of working both independently and collaboratively, with minimal supervision. • Confidentiality: Maintains discretion and handles sensitive information appropriately. • Organizational Skills: Strong time management and problem-solving abilities; able to prioritize and meet deadlines with attention to detail. • Technical Proficiency: Intermediate computer skills, including Microsoft Office and position related software. • Written & Verbal Communication: Strong writing, editing, proofreading, and verbal communication skills. • Background Check: Must pass initial and ongoing background checks as a condition of employment. Work Environment: The work environment involves working for a suburban, Christian university or Christian owned and operated radio station alongside those with a demonstrated commitment and personal relationship with Jesus Christ, a commitment to the mission and values of Northwestern, and an agreement to abide by all Northwestern policies. All applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the United States as we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa. Northwestern's Benefits Overview See Similar Jobs Temporary Custodial Associate Minnesota, United States Physical Plant Responsible for the overall cleanliness of campus buildings on a temporary basis. Assist with maintaining a safe, orderly, and clean environment for students, staff, and visitors. Engagement Specialist/KTIS Minnesota, United States KTIS - St Paul The Engagement Specialist serves as a key representative of KTIS, fostering meaningful connections with listeners through community events, promotions, digital engagement, and outreach initiatives. This role creates impactful brand experiences that advance the station’s mission of leading people to Christ, strengthening listener relationships, and growing community engagement both on-air and in person. Director of Assessment, Academic Affairs Minnesota, United States Dean of Assessmnt & Acad Initiative The Director of Assessment provides strategic leadership for institutional assessment and effectiveness, advancing comprehensive, data-informed practices that support student learning, development, and success across curricular and co-curricular domains. This role partners with academic and administrative units to implement and evaluate systematic assessment processes that strengthen accreditation, continuous improvement, and evidence-based decision-making. Receptionist/KTIS Minnesota, United States KTIS - St Paul 98.5 KTIS, one of the most listened-to radio stations in the Twin Cities, is searching for a receptionist to assist in communicating with listeners and donors.  The right person for this position will enjoy a fast-paced environment while keeping numerous details organized and have a love for people and the mission of KTIS. Traffic Coordinator/KSLT South Dakota, United States KSLT - Rapid City The Traffic Coordinator manages the day-to-day traffic and commercial scheduling functions that keep the station's advertising operations running efficiently and accurately. By coordinating campaign execution, maintaining traffic system integrity, and supporting billing and promotional initiatives, this role contributes directly to the station's financial success, client satisfaction, and overa