    "https://jobs.unwsp.edu/jobs/traffic-coordinator-kslt-south-dakota-united-states": {
      "title": "Traffic Coordinator/KSLT",
      "description": "Traffic Coordinator/KSLT - South Dakota, United States Careers Home Declaration of Christian Community Doctrinal Statement Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Traffic Coordinator/KSLT South Dakota, United States Staff PT Nonexempt Add to favorites View favorites Title: Traffic Coordinator/KSLT VP Area: VP - Media Department: KSLT - Rapid City Position Compensation: $19.00 - $21.81 / hour Location: Rapid City, South Dakota - KSLT Who We Are: Northwestern is a faith-driven community, UNWavering in our Christ-centered principles and identity as those who profess faith in Jesus. Rooted in the unshakable foundation of God’s Word and our calling to impact His world, our mission and vision flow from these core values, expressed through Christ-centered higher education at the University of Northwestern – St. Paul and through gospel outreach and faithfulness with Northwestern Media. Position Summary: The Traffic Coordinator is a part-time position that manages commercial scheduling, billing support, and traffic operations to ensure advertising campaigns are executed accurately and on time. This role works closely with Sales, Programming, and Accounting to maintain accurate records, fulfill client commitments, and support revenue-generating initiatives that advance the station's mission, financial health, and service to advertisers. This is a part-time position scheduled for 20 hours per week. Key Responsibilities: • Manage Commercial Scheduling and Traffic Operations: Oversee the scheduling, placement, and reconciliation of commercial advertising to ensure accurate and timely broadcast delivery. • Maintain Traffic System Accuracy: Ensure the accuracy of sales orders, advertiser information, commercial instructions, and traffic records. • Coordinate Advertising Execution: Work closely with Sales and Programming teams to support the successful implementation of advertising campaigns. • Manage Billing and Accounts Receivable Support: Process advertiser billing and reconcile payments in coordination with accounting functions. • Ensure Compliance with Advertising Agreements: Monitor commercial schedules and materials to ensure campaigns run according to client agreements and station requirements. • Support Station Promotions and Special Events: Provide operational support for station promotions, special events, and other revenue-generating initiatives. • Perform other duties as requested or assigned. Because our community is a significant part of our mission and the development of our students, all employees act as a minister of the gospel of Jesus Christ by actively partnering with the University to disciple students in growing intellectually and spiritually, and with Northwestern Media to lead people to Christ and nurture believers to mature in their faith. Qualifications: Required: • High School diploma or GED • Maintain a growing, personal relationship with Jesus Christ, reflect His character in all interactions, and faithfully uphold and embrace Northwestern’s mission, Doctrinal Statement and Declaration of Christian Community Nice to Have: • Administrative, customer service, office support, or related experience • Experience with radio traffic software and broadcast operations Key Skills: • Independent & Teamwork: Capable of working both independently and collaboratively, with minimal supervision. Ability to interact with a variety of individuals in a kind and professional manner • Confidentiality: Maintains discretion and handles sensitive information appropriately. • Organizational Skills: Strong time management and problem-solving abilities; able to prioritize and meet deadlines with attention to detail and to maintain composure and effectiveness in fast-paced and high-pressure environments. • Technical Proficiency: Intermediate to advanced computer skills, including Microsoft Office and related software. Ability to learn and operate specialized software systems. • Written & Verbal Commun